WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.051
- March 23rd, 2012.

00:00:03.051 --> 00:00:05.634
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.350
I was going to school in Utah.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.024
I was like a junior in college

00:00:11.024 --> 00:00:12.970
studying international relations,

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.860
and I was looking for an internship.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:16.693
Hey, there Iz.

00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:18.310
We're just filming here.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.490
I was on the State Department's website.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.690
The State Department is
like the foreign ministry

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:23.690
here in the United States.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.050
And they had an intro video,
like a promotional video,

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.330
explaining their internship program

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.670
and it was very poorly done.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:36.420
So in a weird moment of, I don't
even know what got into me,

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.380
I sent these people an email and I said.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.137
Well, I said some pretty mean things.

00:00:41.137 --> 00:00:43.760
"I noticed the promo
video you guys are using

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.560
is extremely poorly done.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.300
I would like to make a video that

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.809
is more attractive and helpful."

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:51.860
What!

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.387
Man, 2012, me, was a weird me.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.590
"Lemme know if you would like me

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.160
to make something and submit it.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.320
I just think that this program
could be more attractive

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.450
if the information was presented

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.092
in a more effective way,"

00:01:03.092 --> 00:01:04.520
is how I put it.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.033
Hold on a second, this is 2012.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.990
(dramatic sounds)

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:10.823
Okay.

00:01:10.823 --> 00:01:13.750
I didn't know very much
about video in 2012.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.900
I wasn't making very good videos.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.520
I was making stuff like this,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.410
and like this,

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.040
and it was just not very good.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.550
In addition, I didn't know
how to do motion graphics.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.710
I wanted to learn how to do
it, but I didn't know how.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:32.440
And yet here I am promising
to make a promotional video

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.290
which was very likely
going to be all animation,

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.010
and I had no animation skills.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.040
That's not true actually, to my credit,

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.450
I had one animation under my
belt and it looked like this.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:46.430
That's an owl and a circle
around the owl and it,

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.530
and then it falls and then it goes down,

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.400
it just down.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.840
That was my one portfolio piece.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:55.673
Okay.

00:01:55.673 --> 00:01:59.410
So that's me in 2012, and
yet here I am proposing

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.420
to the State Department
that I'm going to make them

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:06.040
a promotional video that is
quote attractive and helpful.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:06.900
Okay.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:07.733
Cool.

00:02:07.733 --> 00:02:09.200
So, what happens next?

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.520
They responded
enthusiastically and said yes.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.730
If you could make us a video for free

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.800
we would gladly take your
video and put it on our site.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.450
In this moment, something
happened in my brain.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.400
I chalk this up as one of the
inflection points in my life.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.180
It's something that
would continue to happen

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.100
throughout my career and that would

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:33.241
take my animation skills from this,

00:02:33.241 --> 00:02:34.358
to this.

00:02:34.358 --> 00:02:36.941
(upbeat music)

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:42.730
I'm gonna call this process,

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:45.020
this thing that happened, a speed boost.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.550
Just like in Mario Kart, when
you're like cruising along

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.070
and you see those flashy arrows

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:50.077
on the ground and you like hit them

00:02:50.077 --> 00:02:52.683
and it speed boost you forward.

00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:54.780
(car speeding sound)

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:55.613
It's like a hack.

00:02:55.613 --> 00:02:57.780
It's like something that
gives you more speed

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.130
than you naturally have.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.590
After I got that email back
from the State Department,

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.450
I began to devour tutorials.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:07.630
I began to just focus on this
video all day and all night.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.152
I began to learn so much faster

00:03:09.152 --> 00:03:11.520
than I'd ever learned before.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.870
I call this, what was happening to me,

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.660
excited accountability.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:21.070
So after three weeks of
intense, excited accountability

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:25.420
I made this video, my first
real motion graphic project.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.180
Unless you count the owl,
which was technically my first

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.460
and it's pretty dear to my heart.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.313
Love that owl.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.240
Let's face it, when it
comes to internships

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.520
with the State Department
not all college students

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.598
can afford to travel to
Washington DC or overseas.

00:03:38.598 --> 00:03:39.431
Okay.

00:03:39.431 --> 00:03:40.730
I mean, it's not like great.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.820
I went from knowing nothing truly

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.250
to knowing a ton about motion graphics

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.240
and having gotten my hands
dirty for the first time.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.630
And that was facilitated

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.610
through this excited accountability.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:54.770
Soon BSFS will begin the
micro volunteering program.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.050
What's that ask?

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:59.400
Here's a problem, when you
want to learn something new,

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.760
you become passionate about it.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.510
If you wanna learn to bake bread suddenly

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.790
you have a super high
tolerance for reading

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.610
about yeast fermentation.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.010
If you wanna learn photography

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.440
suddenly you're able to sit down and learn

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.910
about shutter speed and aperture,

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.390
these fairly boring principles.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.440
But now you suddenly have

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.070
the attention span of like a genius.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.410
Two weeks goes by and
suddenly that passion,

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.960
that tolerance for boring stuff
becomes thinner and thinner,

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.590
and you eventually pear out.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.540
This was me in 2012.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:30.914
I had made it through a few
weeks of learning this stuff

00:04:30.914 --> 00:04:34.110
when my motivational
fuel started to burn up.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.640
I started to feel less and less inclined

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.140
to actually sit through the tutorials.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:41.170
Then I wrote that email,
I got that response

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:44.330
and this happened (car speeding)

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:45.490
My motivation was back.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:46.680
My tank was full.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:47.680
I was going fast.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.850
I had accountability.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:49.683
I was excited.

00:04:49.683 --> 00:04:53.240
And suddenly my ability to
persist through this kinda

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:56.074
difficult process of learning
increased like tenfold.

00:04:56.074 --> 00:04:58.824
(dramatic music)

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.880
So this is easier said than done.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.500
And a lot of people ask me
like, how do you actually go

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.610
about learning this stuff?

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:07.970
Yeah, you've got the speed boost.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.530
Yeah, you have like
the excited motivation,

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.810
but like what do you
actually do to learn this

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.310
if you don't have film school

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.330
or some sort of structure to learn?

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.240
The answer to me and kind of the key

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.270
to my career when it comes to learning

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.080
this stuff has been the internet.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.760
- [Reporter] On your mark, get set.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:28.270
♪ We're riding on the internet. ♪

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.960
- I have a really soft spot in my heart

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.500
for learning online, and because of that,

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:36.450
I reached out to Skillshare
to sponsor this video.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:37.940
Because Skillshare is one of the sites

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.340
that I've used over the years to learn

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:43.230
and refine my visual storytelling skills.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.840
Skillshare is like this giant
repository of tutorials.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.290
It's like 10 bucks a
month, and you get access

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:53.080
to like 25,000 tutorials.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.190
If you wanna learn animation
like I did in 2012,

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.575
there are tons, tons of
tutorials on the site

00:05:58.575 --> 00:06:01.830
that will teach you all
different aspects of animation.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.520
There's one specifically
called animated infographics

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.720
and data visualization
which was kind of the style

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.340
that I was doing in that, in 2012.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:12.070
It's really good, like quality teaching.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.800
So, if you're kind of in a place right now

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.370
where you want to learn something new,

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.273
whether it's animation or
a million other skills,

00:06:18.273 --> 00:06:21.210
Skillshare has got like
tons of different topics.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.580
Then go click the link, and if you are one

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:27.010
of the first 500, you will
get two months for free.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:27.950
Meaning, you don't have to pay.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.700
And then after that it's 10 bucks a month.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.475
Go start learning stuff.

00:06:31.475 --> 00:06:34.058
(upbeat music)

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.350
Skillshare doesn't have any
influence over this video

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.300
or what I say or anything,
but they did want to partner

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.070
with me on this video
because this is something

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:49.952
that I truly 100% believe in

00:06:49.952 --> 00:06:52.445
and want other people
to experience as well.

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.276
(clock ticking)

00:06:54.276 --> 00:06:55.190
(owl hooting)

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:56.540
(inaudible) don't need to travel abroad.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.170
Okay, so am I recommending
that everyone reach out

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:02.500
to the State Department and
offer to redo their promo video?

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:03.410
No.

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:05.820
This is an example that
illustrates a point

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.272
of putting yourself in a situation

00:07:07.272 --> 00:07:09.390
of excited accountability.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:12.130
First, let's talk about what you need

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:13.830
to make the situation work.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.940
It's right there within
excited accountability.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.260
First you need to be excited.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.950
Whatever situation you put yourself in,

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.760
that's going to teach you these skills.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.490
You have to like be interested in it.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:25.270
You have to align with
whatever the message is

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:26.410
or whatever the project is.

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:28.510
That sort of passion and
excitement about the project

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.520
is going to be a key part of the fuel.

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:32.590
The other aspect of this,
the other side of it

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:33.710
is the accountability part.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:35.960
There needs to be a
good amount of pressure.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.020
Not like the anxiety,
like fear based pressure.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.990
Like, that's actually like a
speed bump, not a speed boost.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.960
I mean the type of pressure
that like you want to deliver

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.690
because you want to impress.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:51.180
And if you don't deliver,
you'll feel a little bit like.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.570
That sort of pressure needs to be there

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.840
'cause that's gonna propel
you forward as well.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:58.360
A good balance of excitement
and accountability

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.660
or pressure together will make
a situation that is primed

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.620
for you to learn and to
have the speed boost.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.940
So lemme give you some examples
that aren't State Department

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:08.620
maybe you want to learn how to cook.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.267
So instead of just like telling yourself,

00:08:10.267 --> 00:08:11.970
"Okay, I wanna learn how to cook."

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.000
You can invite a friend
or some friends over

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.280
for a dinner party and you
are gonna be the one to cook,

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.350
and you tell them that.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.450
If you were interested in
the cuisine or the dish

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:23.440
that you're cooking and you feel

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.680
a little bit of pressure because people

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.730
are coming over to your house,

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.600
suddenly you've just created a situation

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.330
of excited accountability.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:33.170
All right, so let's step up
the stakes one more notch

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:34.880
to a professional level.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.590
Let's say you have some video skills,

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:39.520
but they're not in the place
that you can actually go pitch

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.550
like a brand or an
organization or a news outlet

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:44.470
to make video for them.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.580
You don't have those skills yet,

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.100
but you want to acquire them.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.120
In this case, I suggest
going to a nonprofit

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.530
or a group that doesn't have

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.917
a ton of marketing budget and say,

00:08:53.917 --> 00:08:55.880
"Hey, I will make a video for you."

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:59.250
And you develop a kind of a
pseudo professional relationship

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.060
even though money's not changing hands,

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.270
and it's not that professional,

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:05.180
the stakes are not so high
that if you don't deliver,

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.450
you're like reneging on a contract.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.570
But they're high enough
that you want to deliver.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:10.670
And suddenly you'll be in that

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.830
excited accountability situation,

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:16.700
and here comes the speed
boost.(cartoon car speeding)

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.160
The last example I wanna give you

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.220
is another one that
comes from my experience.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:25.116
Now we're talking summer of 2015.

00:09:25.116 --> 00:09:27.866
(dramatic music)

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.090
Thanks to this excited
accountability process,

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.450
I had done it several times

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.240
with a bunch of different organizations.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.200
I had learned quite a bit of skills

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.150
and I was able to get a
legitimate job in motion graphics.

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:45.500
Eventually that led me
to getting a job at Vox,

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:47.800
where I was doing motion
graphics and animation.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.090
I wanted to take my
skills to the next level.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.840
And specifically I really wanted to get

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.600
into doing documentaries.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.180
I had never done documentaries.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:57.950
I had never made a
legitimate like documentary

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.750
out in the field, but I wanted to learn.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.397
So I went to my boss, at Vox, and I said,

00:10:03.397 --> 00:10:06.700
"Hey, what if I went out
and made an explainer

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.530
like we do here but I did it in the field,

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.400
pointing my camera at
things, getting interviews,

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.910
and then animating on top of that."

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.840
At that time Vox was a startup.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.537
And Joe, my boss, was like,

00:10:15.537 --> 00:10:17.760
"Could you write it, and film it,

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.220
and edit it, and animated
all on your own?"

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.730
And if so, like go for it.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.470
And I was like, "Okay."

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.500
So I pitched this Cuba
story and I was given

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.740
some great support from the people at Vox

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.130
to be able to have, do this experiment.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.687
But the message was very clear.

00:10:34.687 --> 00:10:37.690
"You can do this, but
it needs to be good."

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.860
Meaning if we're gonna
invest in this new format

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:43.160
that's a little bit costlier
to have you go travel to Cuba,

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:47.200
then it has to be like
worth the resources.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:51.209
In the summer of 2015, that
familiar feeling came upon me.

00:10:51.209 --> 00:10:53.010
(cartoon car speeding)

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:57.820
I remember I was sitting
in a hotel in Miami

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.240
the night before I was flying to Cuba.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:03.550
There was $2,000 in
cash sitting on the bed,

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:05.300
because in Cuba they don't take bank cards

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:06.950
you have to like literally
bring a ton of cash,

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:07.990
which is terrifying.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:11.080
And I'm sitting there
with this mandate of,

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.600
if this isn't good it's
not going to happen again,

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:16.800
like 100% responsibility on the situation

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.170
that I've put myself in.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:19.060
Excited.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.640
Yes, I was definitely excited.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:21.930
I mean, look at that face.

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:25.860
That's an excited me,
but also accountable,

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:27.730
pressure, responsibility.

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:30.140
Both of those things were happening to me

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.810
at the most extreme levels

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.180
that they had ever
happened to me in my life.

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:37.150
And there's something
that I can't even explain

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.910
that's just like spilling out of me.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:40.820
I've now done this
process a bunch of times,

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.590
but this was like the most intense.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.650
So that night I did what I had been doing

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:48.740
for weeks up until that moment
which is downloading videos,

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.620
videos that I really loved
from like Vimeo and YouTube,

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:54.130
downloading them and them up in QuickTime

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:58.177
and watching them frame
by frame and writing down,

00:11:58.177 --> 00:11:59.980
"Oh, that edit was really fast,

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:01.560
and it went from this angle to that angle.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:03.770
Oh the guy moved his
camera kind of like this.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:06.140
That was really interesting,
I'm gonna do that in Cuba."

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:09.500
Like a giant list of
exactly what I was gonna do

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.880
to up my skills.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:12.960
Because I was in this highly motivated,

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.200
highly responsible, and
accountable situation

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.720
that learning was sinking in.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:19.870
I was learning in a whole new way.

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:22.370
At the time I watched a Skillshare course

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:24.410
about creative transitions, like how

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:27.740
to move your camera around in
these kinds of creative ways

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:30.900
to build out transitions in your videos.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:34.110
And like I was devouring
this tutorial, like knowing

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:35.710
that I was gonna have to use this stuff

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:38.470
in this situation that I'd put myself in.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.170
I learned so much.

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:43.117
I was so ready to go to Cuba and perform.

00:12:43.117 --> 00:12:45.700
(upbeat music)

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:58.470
In the end I made three
videos and there were the

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.520
best videos that I'd ever made in my life.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:03.970
That was another inflection
point for me, that Cuba trip.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:08.970
I feel grateful to Vox for
giving me that opportunity.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:11.850
Joe, my boss was very, very like open

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.590
to those types of experiments.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.470
And so I'm incredibly
grateful to Vox for that

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:18.690
but I'm also grateful for what
happens to the human brain

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:21.280
when you feel that excited accountability.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.500
You can really really learn a lot

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:25.540
without the need of school.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.730
So thanks to Skillshare
for sponsoring this video,

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:30.070
but also thanks to Skillshare
for just being around,

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.750
for being a repository
of high quality learning

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:34.460
on the internet for 10 bucks a month

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:36.020
so that all of us can access it.

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:38.410
Again if you want to try Skillshare out

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.600
for two months for free,
you can click the link

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.120
down in the description and just see

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.530
if it like is interesting to you.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.980
Good teaching and good
learning, visual learning

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:48.350
like you see on Skillshare
is a way to kind of

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:51.300
help pave that process and
make it a little bit easier.

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:53.840
So, I hope this is helpful.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.130
I would love to hear your
feedback about this process

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.228
and what we talked about today.

00:13:57.228 --> 00:14:01.460
And yeah, I got to go
back to editing borders

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:04.940
because there's just so
much borders to edit.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:05.850
Okay.

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:06.972
Bye.

00:14:06.972 --> 00:14:09.555
(upbeat music)

